some shows go past their prime some  never find their footing and some just  don't do what executives want them to do  from bull to batwoman to babysitters  club a lot of tv shows have already been  canceled in 2022 and we're here to let  you know the reasons why they got the  axe  fitting right in on cbs schedule full of  crime and legal procedurals bull is  about the previously little-known world  of jury consulting inspired by the  former career of talk show host and  executive producer dr phil mcgraw it ran  for six seasons on cbs spending its  first two years among the top 10 most  watched programs on broadcast tv but  then on january 18th 2022 lead actor  michael weatherly tweeted that he was  ready to leave bull and cbs then opted  to cancel the show rather than continue  on without its anchor and besides after  six seasons the show was no longer the  ratings juggernaut it once was ranking  as the eighth most watched cbs drama  among all viewers and dead last in the  sought after 18 to 49 demographic but i  feel confident we can turn that around  in another generation or two  in january 2022 abc launched promised  land a throwback to the primetime soap  operas of the 70s and 80s it was set at  a picturesque california winery  detailing the machinations and romantic  entanglements of several generations of  a sprawling spoiled family alas promised  land brought in the lowest 18 to 49  numbers of any abc drama in the 2021-22  season and it lasted just five episodes  on the prime time schedule subsequent  installments were then dropped directly  on hulu while creator mac lopez claimed  on instagram that the move didn't equal  a cancellation the low ratings and  unceremonious dumping make a second  season highly unlikely  robert langdon is a world-renowned  symbolist the go-to expert for finding  clues in ancient works of art and  historical artifacts to uncover  far-reaching conspiracies he's the hero  of multiple best-selling novels by dan  brown as well as the lost symbol a 2020  peacock original starring ashley  zuckerman as langdon brown's novels were  all massive best sellers and three big  screen adaptations starring tom hanks  earned a worldwide box office of more  than 1.4 billion dollars but each film  made less than the previous and the last  one hit theaters more than five years  before the lost symbol debuted so  perhaps robert langdon's time has simply  passed in january 2022 peacock canceled  the show with a source telling variety  that the streamer and producers figured  they'd told a full story in one season  netflix's hentaipide is set in east los  angeles as it explores the experiences  of latinos trying to make their way in a  gentrifying neighborhood it centers on  the morales family as they keep their  grandfather's restaurant open pursue  their own dreams and fight against the  twin menaces of immigration officials  and gentrification despite early signs  of success including strong critical  notices hentafi traded in quality over  quantity and never attracted a sizable  audience or at least not one large  enough for netflix to justify a third  season the streamer doesn't release  specific viewership numbers for any of  its shows but according to deadline the  second and ultimately final season of  hintified never made an appearance on  the netflix top 10.  ann m martin's beloved babysitter's club  books are cultural touchstones for many  readers who grew up in the 80s and 90s  and lapped up the heartwarming stories  of tween girl small business owners in  suburban connecticut the books have been  adapted before but netflix's version  that debuted in 2020 earned an outsized  amount of praise despite this critical  success the babysitter's club was  cancelled in march 2022 after two  seasons in an interview with vulture  creator rachel shukert revealed that  even though the series pulled in solid  viewership numbers it may not have been  watched in the manner most preferable to  netflix shugert hypothesized that the  streamer wants to devote more resources  to widely appealing shows that are  immediately binge watched upon release  and draw in new markets rather than  quieter shows with a more niche audience  but still  everyone got a little of what they  needed that day  netflix was highly motivated to land  space force which premiered in may 2020  it marked the return to series tv for  steve carell and his reunion with the  office showrunner greg daniels in a  satire of government life during the  donald trump administration carell  played an air force general picked to  head up the fledgling new branch of the  military known as space force the second  season dropped in february 2022 with a  new co-showrunner and production  transferred from los angeles to  vancouver these changes were undertaken  to improve the show's critical quality  and buzz as well as to cut costs the  first season was among the most  expensive shows on contemporary tv but  the viewership figures didn't justify  such an expense especially after april  2022 when netflix reported a massive  subscriber loss and endured a 55 billion  dollar decline in value within a week of  that financial disaster space force was  permanently grounded  batwoman was part of the cw's ambitious  and expansive arrowverse of  interconnected superhero shows initially  starring ruby rose as hero kate kane and  then javicia leslie as criminal turned  caped crusader ryan wilder showrunner  carolyn dries broke the news on twitter  in april 2022 that the show would not be  returning for a fourth season as  reported by variety the cw might be  cleaning house of its underperforming  scripted series as it prepares for an  ownership change it's currently owned by  warner media and viacom cbs with nexstar  media group preparing to buy a majority  stake batwoman was among the least  watched shows on the network in the  2021-2022 season averaging around 760  000 viewers a drop of 20 from the  previous frame  dc's legends of tomorrow follows a  rotating crew of young superheroes  villains and rogues who move through  space time and the universe to prevent  apocalypses and other threats to  humanity it was part of the cw's  arrowverse which dominated the network  in the 2010s but has since been  shrinking in the upcoming 2022 to 2023  season the only shows remaining in the  franchise will be the relatively young  superman and lois and the flash in its  ninth and likely final season legends of  tomorrow was among the oldest and least  popular arrowverse shows concluding  after seven seasons and attracting fewer  viewers than the superhero shows that  survived it reportedly pulled in an  average of just 860 000 watchers in what  wound up being its final season less  than a month after the axe fell the cw  continued to clear out its schedule and  production slate when it canceled seven  more hour-long dramas including dynasty  charmed 4400 roswell new mexico in the  dark legacies and naomi those suckers  are gonna pay for this  countless millennials look back fondly  on the elaborately produced kids game  show legends of the hidden temple like a  mini indiana jones style adventure in a  competitive format the 90s series pitted  six duos against each other as they  raided a supposedly ancient temple  lorded over by a talking stone head  named olmec in search of a priceless  artifact like many fondly remembered 90s  shows legends of the hidden temple  earned a reboot when it arrived on the  cw in october 2021 this revamped bigger  budget version boasts an elaborate set  and features grown-up contestants  instead of kids comedian cristela alonso  hosts while d bradley baker reprises the  role of olmec who remains as eerily  impressive as ever sadly the revamped  legends was met with historically bad  ratings as it reportedly averaged fewer  than 300 000 viewers unsurprisingly then  it was cancelled in june 2022 perhaps  the nostalgia craze that's been gripping  tv lightly is finally over or maybe the  new legends of the hidden temple simply  failed to recapture the original's music  the  2021-2022 season marks the 14th street  year that cbs has been able to call  itself the most watched tv network in  the united states thus compared to other  networks it has higher and more narrow  standards of what constitutes a hit and  which shows are worthy of renewal that  was especially apparent in may 2022 when  cbs canceled one long-running drama and  three sitcoms with middling to low  viewership figures such a culling makes  way for a slew of new series more in  line with the network's hit crime dramas  the axed shows were b-positive united  states of al and how we roll as well as  the magnum pi remake which was later  picked up by nbc at the same time cbs  ordered three new dramas cop show east  new york legal series so help me todd  and firefighter yarn fire country so  help me todd at least sounds like it'll  be good for a laugh every now and then  but you couldn't really call it a comedy  and that's just fine with cbs maybe i  should just let you be  who you want to be  one of the most visually striking sci-fi  shows in recent memory raised by wolves  revolves around two androids mother and  father who are programmed to raise six  human children on a dangerous alien  planet they create a solid space colony  but all their hard work is threatened  when a theological conflict erupts tnt  ordered raised by wolves back in 2018  but it would ultimately premiere on hbo  max in 2020 both seasons of the show  earned strong reviews but the series  couldn't overcome its behind-the-scenes  shuffling in april 2022 warner media and  discovery inc merged to form a new media  company warner brothers discovery  according to raised by wolves star abu  bakr salim this merger brought an early  end to many productions including the  sleek sci-fi show he expressed hope  however that it might be picked up and  continue on another platform if enough  fans push for a rescue  following nancy drew and the hardy boyz  the cw's tom swift was the latest gritty  contemporary reimagining of a  decades-old young adult novel series  loosely based on the books that first  appeared in print in 1910 tian richards  portrayed the title billionaire and tech  genius who wages war with a shadowy  global conspiracy he believes is  responsible for the disappearance of his  father in the books tom swift was a  white teenage inventor while on the show  he's a gay black billionaire in his  twenties but that big change did little  to grab audiences attention the ratings  were strikingly low with a negligible  0.1 rating in the coveted 18-49  demographic as reported by deadline the  show's edgy content may have been what  really led to its demise as nexstar  media group is set to acquire the cw and  reportedly isn't interested in  programming that isn't squeaky clean  debuting in february 2020 fox's  quick-witted animated family sitcom  duncanville arrived packed with talent  co-created by amy poehler and longtime  simpsons writer mike scully the show  revolved around a wildly mediocre but  self-aggrandizing teenage boy named  duncan voiced bipolar a typical episode  featured him bristling against parental  control and hanging out with his crew of  near-duel friends alas duncanville just  couldn't perform at a competitive enough  level for fox which boasts more animated  shows in production than it has space  for on its sunday night animation block  with established hits like the simpsons  bob's burgers and family guy and newer  entries like house broken and the great  north the network also had to make room  for upcoming cartoons gropopolis  produced by community creator dan harmon  and grimsberg starring jon hamm the  ratings for duncanville season 3 were so  bad averaging 530 000 viewers per  episode that fox pulled it off the  schedule and at some point we'll dump  six unaired episodes onto hulu  leaving by  why women kill is a darkly comic crime  anthology detailing the events that led  up to the titular murders debuting on  cbs all access in 2019 the first season  concerned three different time periods  where the same pasadena house and  cheating were involved season two  followed in 2021 on cbs all-access  successor paramount plus with a  standalone story about a new character  driven to commit homicide  in december 2021 paramount plus ordered  a new set of episodes of why women kill  the show reportedly placed high on a top  10 list of the streamers most popular  and visible programs the new slate of  episodes went into pre-production but  then on july 1 2022 paramount plus  reversed course and decided that it  didn't want any more y women kill after  all and cancel the series after just two  seasons  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one

